# Test: enum-refusal-set-format
#
# QUESTION: does `ze config validate` of a set-format file refuse an enum
# value, a leaf-list member and a list key with the same operator error as a
# hierarchical file, framed for the set line: the line, the full path, the
# values with help, and a fix that is the line retyped with the refused word
# replaced (the line's own verb, `nop` on a `nop` line), the rest of the line
# kept? A unit test drives the set parser over a test schema; this drives the
# shipped YANG through DetectFormat and the real printer.
#
# Leaves:
#   bgp peer <name> session capability route-refresh, typedef capability-mode
#     (internal/component/bgp/yang/ze-bgp-conf.yang).
#   ospf router-information scope, leaf-list of an enumeration
#     (internal/plugins/ospf/yang/ze-ospf-conf.yang).
#   ospf redistribute <source>, list key `source`, an enumeration
#     (internal/plugins/ospf/yang/ze-ospf-conf.yang).
#
# Producers: framedRefusal, valueLineRefusal, keyLineRefusal and lineVerb
# (internal/component/config/setparser_refusal.go).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-config-enum-refusal-proposes-valid-values AC-24 (set, set-meta
#   and nop lines), AC-5 set-format leaf-list member, AC-25 set-format key with
#   the rest of the line kept, and the key-only line.
# PREVENTS: `invalid value for ...`, `invalid key for ...`, `invalid enum`, or
#   a fix written in the file form inside a set-format file.

stdin=leaf:terminator=EOF_LEAF
set bgp router-id 203.0.113.253
set bgp peer peer1 connection remote ip 192.0.2.1
set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh requre
EOF_LEAF

stdin=meta:terminator=EOF_META
#thomas @local %2026-04-21T12:34:56Z set bgp router-id 203.0.113.253
#thomas @local %2026-04-21T12:34:56Z set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh requre
EOF_META

stdin=nop:terminator=EOF_NOP
set bgp router-id 203.0.113.253
set bgp peer peer1 connection remote ip 192.0.2.1
nop bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh requre
EOF_NOP

stdin=member:terminator=EOF_MEMBER
set ospf router-id 10.0.0.1
set ospf router-information scope bogus
EOF_MEMBER

stdin=key:terminator=EOF_KEY
set ospf router-id 10.0.0.1
set ospf redistribute bogus nssa-propagate true
EOF_KEY

stdin=keyonly:terminator=EOF_KEYONLY
set ospf router-id 10.0.0.1
set ospf redistribute bogus
EOF_KEYONLY

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=leaf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 3: bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh: "requre" is not an accepted value (did you mean require?)
expect=stdout:pattern=route-refresh accepts only these values:\n +enable   Advertise the capability; no enforcement\n +disable  Do not advertise the capability; no enforcement\n +require  Advertise the capability; refuse the session when the peer does not offer it\n +refuse   Do not advertise the capability; refuse the session when the peer offers it\n *fix: set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh require
reject=stdout:contains=invalid value for
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum
reject=stdout:contains=expected one of
reject=stdout:contains=fix: route-refresh

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=meta
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 2: bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh: "requre" is not an accepted value (did you mean require?)
expect=stdout:contains=fix: set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh require
reject=stdout:contains=invalid value for
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=nop
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 3: bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh: "requre" is not an accepted value (did you mean require?)
expect=stdout:contains=fix: nop bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh require
reject=stdout:contains=fix: set bgp
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=member
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 2: ospf router-information scope: "bogus" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:pattern=scope accepts only these values:\n +link  Link-local
expect=stdout:contains=fix: set ospf router-information scope <link|area|as>
reject=stdout:contains=(valid:
reject=stdout:contains=invalid value for
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum

cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=key
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 2: ospf redistribute bogus: "bogus" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:pattern=source accepts only these values:\n +connected  Routes of the addresses configured on local interfaces\.
expect=stdout:contains=fix: set ospf redistribute <connected|static|kernel|bgp|isis> nssa-propagate true
reject=stdout:contains=invalid key for
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum

cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=keyonly
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 2: ospf redistribute bogus: "bogus" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:pattern=fix: set ospf redistribute <connected\|static\|kernel\|bgp\|isis>\n*$
reject=stdout:contains=invalid key for
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum
